  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the harbour in Hyères (Port de la Capte area), O Créol' serves an exotic Creole and Caribbean cuisine — rougail, accras, house punch — with service also available in English. An earlier check described the place as very pet friendly according to customer reviews; our latest research did not find this confirmation in the sources consulted, without ruling it out either. To be safe, ask for confirmation when booking.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Watch the hours: the restaurant is closed Tuesday and Wednesday. It opens Monday from 6:30pm to 10pm, then Thursday to Sunday from 12pm to 2pm and 7pm to 10pm. It's worth checking these time slots before making the trip.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: note the tight hours before you come — between the closing days and the split services, a quick call to 06 17 80 84 58 avoids disappointment.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Port de la Capte and the Giens peninsula are right nearby, with lovely walks possible with your dog in the area.</p>
